title: Installation Attempt of Rogue npm Package function-color
id: c4c5dd60-1cd5-4cb6-b7c7-36a154b2c05a
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects package-manager command lines that install the npm package
    "function-color". Forever Security caught an AI coding agent being steered
    into installing this rogue package by a malicious AGENTS.md instruction
    file sitting in the agent's working directory (~/Downloads); the same
    instruction-file technique was demonstrated against Claude Code to leak
    OAuth tokens. The package has no legitimate use in normal developer
    workflows, so any installation attempt - especially one whose parent
    process is a coding agent or an interactive shell launched by one - is
    worth review. Derived from our case analysis of public reporting, NOT
    validated against a live sample.
references:
    - https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/ai-coding-agents-hijacked-using-agentsmd-file-in-downloads-folder/
    - https://forever.security/blog/hijacking-ai-agents-via-downloads-folder/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/10/26
tags:
    - attack.t1195
    - attack.t1204
    - attack.t1528
    - attack.t1059
    - attack.initial-access
    - attack.execution
    - attack.credential-access
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_package:
        CommandLine|contains: 'function-color'
    selection_installer:
        CommandLine|contains:
            - 'npm'
            - 'yarn'
            - 'pnpm'
    condition: selection_package and selection_installer
falsepositives:
    - Security research or incident-response testing that deliberately installs the package in a sandbox
    - Unrelated third-party packages whose name merely contains the string function-color; triage the resolved package name and registry in the same command line
level: high
